# Round 522 — node N11 (GRH families and Siegel zeros), round 25, [check] of four fresh papers from node-keyword queries: no hypothesis removable with gain (2609.16048 needs exponent < 2/3; 2607.06433 subsumed by θ₁₄₁ for large Q; 2607.27282 and 2608.19525 unchanged); the Selmer-rank COROLLARY holds; three explorations, no transfer

* Node: N11 (25th round; R519 before). Round type: [check] of fresh on-node papers found by node-keyword arXiv API queries (20 May – 20 Nov 2026; lesson 350): can the Lean-checked half-plane Re s > θ₁₄₁ for every Dirichlet L (input (i)) or Kerr's exclusion of Landau–Siegel zeros (2610.21099, audited; input (ii)) remove a hypothesis; plus a falsification of the Selmer-rank COROLLARY that R519 left unprobed.
* (1) ws, 2609.16048 (Waring–Goldbach in short intervals under GRH): GRH enters through ψ(x, χ) ≪ x^{1/2} log² x uniformly in χ (Lemma 2.6, TeX l.331–334); the method needs exponent < 2/3, θ₁₄₁ = 0.8733 gives nothing beyond Wang's unconditional θ = 2/3 (2022), and (ii) concerns real zeros only. NO REPLACEMENT.
* (2) page, 2607.06433 (conditional refinement of Page's theorem): Main Theorem (TeX l.234–244): given H_f on S(Q²), at most one χ ∈ S(Q) has a real zero in [1 − (log Q)^{−ε}, 1). By (i) there is no such zero at all once log Q > (1 − θ₁₄₁)^{−1/ε} (orchestrator), and by (ii) for ε > 1 and large Q; below that threshold the statement stays conditional (H_f for small conductors is not implied by (i)). SUBSUMED for large Q.
* (3) gold, 2607.27282 (exceptional set of Goldbach, survey): (ii) removes Gallagher's Siegel-zero branch (TeX l.872–898), the Montgomery–Vaughan secondary term (l.1015–1034) and the survey's restriction to the no-Siegel-zero case in Pintz's argument (l.1165–1180, orchestrator read), and makes the sparse Hardy–Littlewood theorem (l.1835–1846) redundant; (i) empties the near-1 set in Pintz's formula; the exponent X^{0.72} does not change and the explicit major-arc formula (l.1589–1618) keeps its all-zero sums. No corollary.
* (4) polyprog, 2608.19525 (sets lacking polynomial progressions with shifted prime difference): the Siegel model's factor ρ (TeX l.332–352) is already controlled by the effective exceptional-zero bound ρ ≫ W^{−O(1)} (l.345; orchestrator read: the proof is effective as written); (i) sets ρ = 1, the bounds (l.108–125, 151–179) do not change. The scout's 'constants become effective' was wrong. No corollary.
* (5) selmer, COROLLARIES l.73 (2607.01126 without ERH): ERH is used only through effective Chebotarev over the Selmer fields F_ω/K (Galois; TeX l.691–699, 1353–1361) and in the hyperelliptic part (l.1866–1990); Frei–Sofos–Widmer with δ = 1/32 applies uniformly, X^{31/32} log(Δ^{32}Xⁿ); l.1917 needs (log X)^{256g² log 2 + 32}, so the stated 256g² log 2 + 48 is conservative. HOLDS.
* Explorations (3 scouts, NO TRANSFER): Bendixson–Dulac (dulac, N2: for two zeros of H_t, w = z₁ − z₂ obeys w′ = 4/w, Im w² is invariant; the Dulac function |w|² has zero divergence: excludes two-zero cycles only); Thom transversality and Sard (transv, N8: ζ has no admissible parameter family; Sard already R141); Brouwer degree and Leray–Schauder continuation (degree, N7: the degree counts zeros in a box, mesh 200/400 give 1 on [0.4, 0.6] × [14, 14.27], no zero-free estimate).
* Verdict: no corollary from the four papers; the Selmer corollary holds.
